  "source_caption": "Kanye West doing a rehearsal of Through The Wire with the ARC Choir (2004)\n\n In the early 2000s, Kanye West was captured rehearsing “Through The Wire” with the Addicts Rehabilitation Center (ARC) Gospel Choir a Harlem based group made up of recovering addicts. The ARC Choir was originally founded in 1957 by James Allen as part of a rehabilitation program that used gospel music as therapy and a form of spiritual healing. The group had previously recorded “Walk With Me” in 1997, which Kanye famously sampled for “Jesus Walks” on his 2004 debut album The College Dropout.\n\n[join the community @uneedmink]",
